PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The unanimous group consensus firmly identifies the letter formed by Istituto Galilei-Pacinotti and Liceo Ulisse Dini as "H". Cadastral and aerial evidence confirms two parallel multi-story classroom wings connected at their midpoint by an orthogonal transversal block containing shared facilities. Competing claims regarding the letter "M" have been thoroughly refuted as geometric impossibilities and instances of post-war architectural folklore (pareidolia mussoliniana), as the complex was constructed in the late 1960s. The conclusion of "H" remains solid and finalized heading into the final deliberation round.
}

